==Latin==

===Etymology===
Of {{unc|la|nocap=1}} origin;<ref name=EDL>{{R:itc:EDL|page=660|head=vēna}}</ref><ref>{{R:la:WH|head=vena|page=746|vol=2}}</ref> proposed derivations include:
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*weǵʰ-|t=to bring, transport}}, the same root of {{m|la|via|t=road}}.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*wenh₁-|t=to love}}, the same root of {{m|la|venēnum|t=[[juice]]; [[venom]]}}.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*weyp-|t=to shake, swing}}, the same root of {{m|la|vibex|t=weal, welt}}.
* From a root common to {{cog|lt|gýsla|t=vein}} and {{cog|ru|жи́ла||vein}}.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*h₂weh₁-|t=to blow}}, as veins are similar to air pipes.
* From {{der|la|ine-pro|*wedʰ-|t=to pledge, lead}}.
* From a {{der|la|ine-pro||*wes-no-|t=of blood}}, and cognate with {{cog|ae|𐬬𐬀𐬢𐬵𐬎𐬙𐬁𐬝|t=blood}}, as well as perhaps {{cog|sa|वसा|t=fat, lard}}. This theory appears to be preferred by De Vaan.<ref name=EDL />

