===Etymology===
First attested in Dutch-language newspapers in Suriname in the 1930s. Possibly a {{clipping|srn|patapeido|nocap=1}}, of unclear origin; since the term is first attested in the 20th century with the specific meaning 'canvas shoe', proposed derivations from {{ncog|pt|sapato||(leather) shoe}}, {{ncog|pt|pata||paw, foot}}, or {{ncog|yo|bàta||(leather) shoe}} seem unlikely.<ref>{{cite-journal|nl
|author=w:Nicoline van der Sijs
|title=Etymologica: Patta’s
|journal=Neerlandistiek
|publisher={{w|Meertens Institute}}/{{w|Instituut voor de Nederlandse Taal}}
|date=5 December 2022
